      "body": "@JICA98 \n\ninstalled i22 release, saw in settings for installation media and chose sd card. Selected Import and folder in main screen/library. Validation completes and goes into importing the game folder. After importing is done, the game lists in the main screen/library then the app becomes unresponsive and option to \"wait\" or \"close app\" appear. I tried wait a few times and closed app. When the app was closed and reopened the game wasnt in the main screen/library anymore and the app is unresponsive requiring to close. \n\ni saw the bachata folder in the android folder on the sd card, and saw that the game folder was copied into this bachata folder. \n\nbecause of the app crashing, i uninstalled the app and reinstalled and imported the game again. instead of closing the bachata app this time i chose the game bloodborne and it started up, made it past the character creation screen and the app crashed. upon opening bachata again the app immediately is unresponsive and the bloodborne import is gone but the game still exists in sdcard>android>data>bachata>files>games>CUSA00900",
